David Damerell wrote:
> 
> On reflection, however, I don't think there is any real prospect that a
> Croesus-reaching character can't do _something_ about the moat,

Yes, there are indeed many many options to pass water. The guaranteed
items are the scrolls of earth from Sokoban and the Castle wand as a
joker to wish for almost everything to pass the moat. You could even
smash the entry door with striking or force bolt and jump into the
moat; then, I suspect, you'll occasionally reach the castle doorway;
with less effective rusted gear if one doesn't mind that degradation.
An angry giant with a boulder is nicer, therefore, or a random wand
of cold that a soldier might have dropped.

Otherwise the objects you find depend, as usual, on the RNG. (Been
there. Needed the scrolls of earth to pass Medusa. Had no boots, no
potions, none of the countless other options.)

Anyway, the most interesting incentive on Croesus' level (you should
have reflection to enter) are the dragons to obtain appropriate armor
and some types of wands (death, fire, lightning) from the soldiers.
Entering Croesus' castle was rarely necessary in my games.

> even if it is just a blessed PoLev and a careful count of turns.

A single blessed potion of levitation is not too useful; why enter
Croesus' castle if you cannot pick things up? Levitation will also,
I assume, prevent you from sitting on the throne.

